[162.271694, "o", "\r\n=== Context around line 154 ===\r\nLine 151: j=1\r\nLine 152: j̸=i\r\nLine 153: 1\r\nLine 154: (xi−xj)2·sgn (xi−xj) (1)\r\nLine 155: where ∆V is the voltage difference between the be-\r\nLine 156: ginning and the end of a step,t is the time after the\r\n\r\n=== Context around line 173 ===\r\nLine 170: photon source [? ]. The probability of two-photon corre-\r\nLine 171: lationwhendetectingacorrelationeventontwodetectors\r\nLine 172: at different times is given by\r\nLine 173: ρc(τ) =ρ1(τ)ρ2(τ+δT), (2)\r\nLine 174: where ρ1(τ) and ρ2(τ+δT) are the probability of de-\r\nLine 175: tecting a photon att =τand τ+δTon detector 1 and\r\n\r\n=== Context around line 229 ===\r\nLine 226: am +a†\r\nLine 227: m\r\nLine 228: )]\r\nLine 229: , (3)\r\nLine 230: where Ω (i) istheRabifrequencyofthe ithion, am anda†\r\nLine 231: m\r\n\r\n=== Context around line 254 ===\r\nLine 251: Ω (i)\r\nLine 252: n t\r\nLine 253: )]\r\nLine 254: , (4)\r\nLine 255: wherePn is the occupation on thenth number state and\r\nLine 256: encodes a convolution between a thermal and a coher-\r\n"]
