[168.678328, "o", "Line 156: ginning and the end of a step,t is the time after the\r\nLine 157: end of the previous step, and T = 9.1 µs is the total\r\nLine 158: time of each transport. The details of voltage optimiza-\r\nLine 159: tion and numerical simulation of motional heating can\r\n\r\n=== EQUATION (3) - wider context ===\r\nLine 215: fects the ion-motion (Fig.??). The carrier Rabi flopping\r\nLine 216: is motional state sensitive, and the Hamiltonian has the\r\nLine 217: form of [? ? ]\r\nLine 218: Hi,M = (ℏ/2)Ω (i)σ(i)\r\nLine 219: x\r\nLine 220: M∏\r\nLine 221: m=1\r\nLine 222: exp\r\nLine 223: [\r\nLine 224: iηi,m\r\nLine 225: [\r\nLine 226: am +a†\r\nLine 227: m\r\nLine 228: )]\r\nLine 229: , (3)\r\nLine 230: where Ω (i) istheRabifrequencyofthe ithion, am anda†\r\nLine 231: m\r\nLine 232: are the creation and annihilation operators on themth\r\nLine 233: mode, andηi,m istheLDparameterofthe ithionandthe\r\nLine 234: mth mode. Considering the computational difficulty of\r\n\r\n=== EQUATION (4) - wider context ===\r\nLine 240: Rabi flopping can be simplified to\r\nLine 241: Pe(t) = 1\r\nLine 242: 2N\r\nLine 243: [\r\nLine 244: 1−\r\n"]
[168.678372, "o", "Line 245: ∞∑\r\nLine 246: n=0\r\nLine 247: N∑\r\nLine 248: i=0\r\nLine 249: Pn cos\r\nLine 250: (\r\n"]
[168.678405, "o", "Line 251: Ω (i)\r\nLine 252: n t\r\nLine 253: )]\r\nLine 254: , (4)"]
[168.678435, "o", "\r\nLine 255: wherePn is the occupation on thenth number state and\r\nLine 256: encodes a convolution between a thermal and a coher-\r\nLine 257: ent phonon distribution [? ]. Ω (i)\r\n"]
[168.67862, "o", "Line 258: n is the Rabi frequency\r\nLine 259: of the ith ion on thenth number state [? ]. To ver-\r\n"]
